#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0068 expect=violation domain=DS
#note "Round 2026-10-15, ruling D130 (owner 2026-09-17: the derivation copy must EQUAL the value min_date / max_date selected -- compare as TEXT): the date() wrappers are gone, so P2 (precision: day vs datetime of the same day) and P3 (the same instant with and without a UTC offset) now FIRE -- the copy is not the selected value -- and the scenario expects FOUR violations. Before D130: Four probes for the D100/SPEC 5.2 retyping (phase 3c, RUNBOOK-phase3c-corpus-rewrite.md 6.2). Subject P1 is the positive: the earliest informed-consent DSSTDTC genuinely differs from DM.RFICDTC at day precision. P2 and P3 FIRE under plain string equality and are SILENT under typed date equality -- P2 precision (day vs datetime of the same day), P3 UTC offset (same instant spelled with and without an offset). P4 is the UNPOSITIONABLE probe (calendar-impossible RFICDTC): it was silent from the phase-3c rewrite until H1b and FIRES AGAIN since -- owner ruling 2026-09-17, SPEC 5.2(4) amended (<meta>/.claude/docs/specs/SPEC-typed-expression-engine.md): an unbounded hull answers `negate`, so date_not_equal_to fires on an unpositionable operand in EITHER position. That is the right answer here: RFICDTC 2026-02-99 is not a date at all, so it is certainly not the earliest informed-consent DSSTDTC 2026-01-01, and the rule now says so; the finding lands on the DS row carrying that earliest value. So this scenario expects TWO violations, P1 and P4. This scenario is red on the pre-rewrite corpus by construction."
#expectViolationCount 4
#expectViolationAt row=1 USUBJID=P1
#expectViolationAt row=3 USUBJID=P2
#expectViolationAt row=5 USUBJID=P3
#expectViolationAt row=7 USUBJID=P4
dataset DS label=Disposition
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col DSDECOD type=Char label="Standardized Disposition Term"
col DSSTDTC type=Char label="Start Date/Time of Disposition Event"
---
S1 | DS | P1 | INFORMED CONSENT OBTAINED | 2026-01-01
S1 | DS | P1 | INFORMED CONSENT OBTAINED | 2026-01-05
S1 | DS | P2 | INFORMED CONSENT OBTAINED | 2026-01-01T09:00
S1 | DS | P2 | INFORMED CONSENT OBTAINED | 2026-01-05
S1 | DS | P3 | INFORMED CONSENT OBTAINED | 2026-01-01T09:00
S1 | DS | P3 | INFORMED CONSENT OBTAINED | 2026-01-05
S1 | DS | P4 | INFORMED CONSENT OBTAINED | 2026-01-01
S1 | DS | P4 | INFORMED CONSENT OBTAINED | 2026-01-05
---

dataset DM label=Demographics
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col RFICDTC type=Char label="Date/Time of Informed Consent"
